<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n113133" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκό-κροτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sounding</i> or
				<i>rattling with bronze,</i> epith. of Demeter, in allusion to
			instruments used in her worship, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				7(6).3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χ. ἵπποι</span> horses <i>that
				stamp with hoofs of bronze, brazen-hoofed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				552
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκήλατος, φάσγανον</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				1577
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκόκροτα</span>”
				<i>bronze utensils,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					POxy.
					1657.1
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκοκρότος, ὁ,</span>
			= Lat. <i>aerarius,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλκόκροτος</span> cod.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
